1
00:00:00,039 --> 00:00:05,360
In Unit, open Maps and find the Community
coordination centre under Indoor Maps.

2
00:00:05,829 --> 00:00:07,469
Select that indoor entry.

3
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:10,659
The viewer opens with Ground floor
selected in blue.

4
00:00:11,119 --> 00:00:15,170
The row beneath the Indoor Maps heading
lets you switch between this floor plan

5
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:17,260
and the department’s other saved layers.

6
00:00:17,670 --> 00:00:21,360
This fictional example is for reviewing
reference information with a crew.

7
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,810
On Ground floor, inspect the floor-plan
image and the shaded room area.

8
00:00:26,179 --> 00:00:27,730
Select that shaded area.

9
00:00:28,179 --> 00:00:32,200
A card opens with the saved name, Briefing
room, and its description.

10
00:00:32,579 --> 00:00:35,419
Read the card before relying on a short
map label.

11
00:00:35,759 --> 00:00:39,159
The image and the selectable room overlay
are separate pieces of

12
00:00:39,159 --> 00:00:42,259
reference information that should agree
with the reviewed plan.

13
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:44,739
Select the G I S import tab.

14
00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:48,849
This layer shows two imported region
overlays on the floor image.

15
00:00:49,189 --> 00:00:53,679
Select the training-room area to open its
saved Training room import details.

16
00:00:54,070 --> 00:00:56,879
Changing a tab changes the layer you are
inspecting.

17
00:00:57,280 --> 00:01:01,199
Check the selected blue tab and the opened
region’s name together so you

18
00:01:01,199 --> 00:01:03,260
are discussing the intended reference.

19
00:01:03,389 --> 00:01:05,279
Enter Equipment in the search field.

20
00:01:05,649 --> 00:01:08,720
The matching equipment overlay remains
while the other region

21
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:09,919
overlay is filtered out.

22
00:01:10,309 --> 00:01:13,860
The room names printed inside the
floor-plan image remain visible

23
00:01:13,910 --> 00:01:16,700
because that image is separate from the
searchable overlay.

24
00:01:17,130 --> 00:01:20,519
Select the matching shaded area to open
Equipment import and

25
00:01:20,519 --> 00:01:22,060
review its saved description.

26
00:01:22,489 --> 00:01:26,769
Search helps focus the display; it does
not change the saved floor drawing.

27
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:30,279
Close the detail card and remove Equipment
from the search field.

28
00:01:30,769 --> 00:01:34,099
Both region overlays return on the G I S
import layer.

29
00:01:34,559 --> 00:01:38,659
Clear a search when handing the device to
another crew member so the restricted view

30
00:01:38,689 --> 00:01:40,819
is not mistaken for the complete layer.

31
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:44,420
Select the K M L and K M Z import tab.

32
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:48,639
This data layer displays the two imported
areas over the base map,

33
00:01:48,820 --> 00:01:50,420
without the floor-plan image.

34
00:01:50,779 --> 00:01:54,239
Select each area and read its saved name
and description.

35
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:58,130
The dispatchable area also offers Dispatch
to this zone.

36
00:01:58,589 --> 00:02:02,019
This walkthrough reviews the reference
cards without submitting a call.

37
00:02:02,410 --> 00:02:05,630
Verify the selected area and your
department’s call procedure

38
00:02:05,630 --> 00:02:07,589
before using a dispatch action.

39
00:02:07,830 --> 00:02:11,240
Return to Maps and reopen the same Indoor
Maps entry.

40
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:15,140
Ground floor and the saved room overlay
return in this example.

41
00:02:15,609 --> 00:02:19,959
These are stored reference locations; this
viewer does not show who is inside

42
00:02:19,959 --> 00:02:22,220
a room or confirm physical arrival.

43
00:02:22,650 --> 00:02:27,290
Community paramedicine and mental health
teams, search-and-rescue crews, security

44
00:02:27,290 --> 00:02:32,339
departments, wildland contractors and
industrial response teams can use reviewed

45
00:02:32,339 --> 00:02:35,139
site references alongside fire and E M S.

46
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:39,389
Keep the map current and verify
live-location information separately.

